& [RustSurface]
  + add evox2_remote_preflight_private_permit_bridge as a pub(crate) module declaration in cantor_ecosystem lib with no pub mod no pub use and no public re-export
  + add one pub(crate) opaque live-admission type one private bridge core one pub(crate) unreachable production bridge entry and one pub(crate) terminal outcome type with private fields
  + add exactly one pub(crate) permit-issuance function inside the existing runner module and leave existing permit fields runner entry backend process and receipt semantics unchanged
  + add no binary CLI environment-variable dispatcher feature-gated dispatcher trait-object registry alternate process implementation or ambient route

& [OpaqueAdmission]
  + carries exact activation request proposal proposal-verification operator-decision correspondence producer-plan and observed-time identities plus pinned implementation bookends and ceilings
  + decision kind is authorize fixture_only is false maximum attempts permits runner entries and processes are one and retry count is zero
  + has private fields and no Clone Copy Default Serialize Deserialize public constructor production factory machine form durable representation logging or recovery path
  + no production admission constructor exists in bridge implementation; only a later separately governed nested live_initiation child module may add one

& [PermitIssuance]
  + PB1 validates activation request proposal verification decision correspondence producer plan exact lineages effect accounts and nonfixture authorize semantics before issuance
  + PB2 moves the opaque admission into the one runner issuer which rechecks its fixed coordinates and constructs the existing three-private-field permit exactly once
  + rejected absent malformed mismatched stale future replayed ambiguous fixture or otherwise unadmitted inputs stop before PB2 with permits0 runner entries0

& [ConsumeAndInvoke]
  + PB3 returns the one permit only to the private bridge lexical scope
  + PB4 immediately moves that permit into one FnOnce runner call using the existing request plan program and producer plan
  + no operation between issuance and the runner call may clone serialize persist return replace refresh inspect for logging or expose the permit
  + the bridge contains no loop recursion retry queue re-entry fallback or second runner target

& [ReceiptAndTerminal]
  + PB5 on runner success serializes with the existing canonical runner serializer reparses with the existing strict runner parser validates the reparsed receipt and requires byte-identical canonical reserialization
  + PB6 returns exactly one non-capability terminal outcome completed_available completed_provider_unavailable abandoned_after_consumption or receipt_refused
  + provider-unavailable remains a successful verified preflight observation with provider requests0 remote calls1 effects1 and synthetic trials0
  + any runner error after issuance becomes abandoned_after_consumption even when the runner reports a pre-spawn refusal; no admission permit or retry authority returns
  + receipt parsing validation digest or byte mismatch becomes receipt_refused and cannot be promoted to completion
  + every PB3-or-later terminal carries permit_consumed true runner_invocations1 and has no outgoing transition

& [ProviderFreeFixture]
  + unit tests reside as a child of the private bridge module so they may directly construct private admission literals without a constructor helper or exported backdoor
  + a private generic core accepts one FnOnce mock runner closure; tests never call the production bridge entry existing physical runner contained process OpenSSH or EVO-X2
  + fixture outcomes are explicitly synthetic and carry formation and implementation runner invocations0 process spawns0 provider requests0 remote calls0 effects0

& [StaticAbsence]
  + reject public module or re-export admission constructor derives or impls for Clone Copy Default Serialize Deserialize admission or permit machine forms bridge binaries ambient dispatch alternate process calls retry loops and live_initiation code
  + reject any second permit constructor issuer runner entry bridge entry or path that returns admission or permit
  + static gates are reviewed-tree evidence only and must be rerun after every relevant change

